/**
 * NOTE: loading this external script and then calling classes/methods on it is pretty tricky due to anonymous define() calls present in script, after requireJS has already been loaded
 *  - the trick here is to load the external script via require.config(), and then call require() passing in dependencies, BUT DO NOT call library within require()
 *     -- require() should be empty, and library calls should be placed OUTSIDE require() -- (which obviously means using vanilla JS instead of jQuery)
 *       --> I don't know WHY this works... but it does
 *
 * ADDITIONAL INFO:
 *  - calling library from inside require() makes library class methods inaccessible (e.g. Calendly.showPopupWidget())
 *  - excluding the empty require() call makes library classes inaccessible (e.g. Calendly)
 *
 */
?>

